cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Eddy AI, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Eddy AI: a plug-and-play controller that wraps any robot's existing code"
type: software
# TODO before release: replace with real names (family-names / given-names), add the
# supervisor and any other contributors, and add ORCID iDs if you have them.
authors:
  - alias: myseiv
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
repository-code: "https://github.com/myseiv/eddy_ai"
keywords:
  - robotics
  - ROS 2
  - robot control
  - multi-robot systems
  - plug and play
abstract: >-
  Eddy attaches to a robot's existing software without modifying it, works out what the
  robot can do (from a live ROS 2 graph and URDF, or a self-describing serial/TCP line
  protocol), and accepts one set of commands on every robot: typed, spoken offline, hand
  signs, programmatic, or from another robot. It runs without a language model, checks every
  command against the robot's limits and sensors, and lets robots coordinate peer to peer
  with signed messages.
